text:
Maya: Heads up — noticed a few broken links + an unclear example in the function/tool-calling docs after the last merge. Can we triage?
Jon: which page? link(s)?
Maya: /docs/guides/tool-integration.md — the JSON schema example references a `response_schema` prop that doesn't exist anymore. Also the SDK snippet uses `callTool()` from v0.9, we now have `invokeTool()` in v1.x.
Liam: ah — that explains the CI lint failures I've been seeing. I can patch the snippet to v1 API.
Sara: I can take the schema example. Do we want to show both legacy and new schema shapes, or only the new pattern?
Maya: prefer only new pattern to avoid confusion, but add a small migration note: "If you're upgrading from v0.x, replace response_schema -> outputSchema and callTool -> invokeTool" (inline).
Jon: +1. Also add a short note about guardrails: recommend using `type: object` with `additionalProperties: false` for strict parsing, and a short example of parsing failure handling.
Liam: assembling a quick patch. Proposed SDK snippet:
```js
// v1 invokeTool example
const res = await client.invokeTool('summarizer', {
  input: 'long article text',
  options: { maxTokens: 300 }
});
console.log(res.output);
```
Sara: for the schema snippet I drafted:
```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "summary": {"type": "string"},
    "highlights": {"type": "array", "items": {"type":"string"}}
  },
  "required": ["summary"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```
Jon: perfect. Can we also add a tiny example of programmatic parse-checking in the SDK so folks don't blindly trust generated output? e.g.:
```js
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(res.output);
  validateSchema(parsed, schema); // returns true/throws
} catch (err) {
  // fallback: call model again or return a safe default
}
```
Maya: yes — and add a short blurb about `prefix caching` side effects when using deterministic tool outputs (helps avoid stale KV issues) — just a one-liner linking to the caching guide.
Jon: I can add the link. FYI I fixed the two broken links in the TOC as part of the branch.
Liam: pushed a branch `docs/tooling-snippets-v1` with the SDK updates and the parse-check example. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/482
Sara: pushed `docs/schema-strictify` with the schema example + migration note. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/483
Maya: awesome. Can Docs Bot run the link-checker + schema validation job?
Docs Bot: Scheduled: docs/link-check (priority: high) and docs/schema-lint on PRs #482 and #483.
Jon: CI showed one failing test on #483 — a markdown rendering edge case with fenced code titles. I fixed it in the branch.
Liam: I'll re-run the preview deploy afterwards. DeployBot: queued preview build for PR #482 and #483.
DeployBot: preview up at https://preview.docs.redwood.ai/pr-482-483/ (expires in 48h)
Maya: quick review plan: Jon approve the final wording for guardrails; Sara confirm schema JSON is copy-paste ready; Liam confirm SDK snippet passes lint. Then merge.
Jon: I'll review now and aim to approve in the hour.
Sara: schema is copy-paste ready, added an extra test case in the fixtures folder.
Liam: snippet lints clean. one minor var rename that I pushed.
Maya: thanks team. After merge, can someone add a short migration note to the changelog? small bullet under "docs" in the release notes.
Jon: I'll add it.
Maya: closing loop — tagging this thread to the release checklist. :white_check_mark:
